<section class="sos-band">
  <div class="wrap sos">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">If it goes wrong</p>
      <h2 style="margin-block:12px 18px">Somebody knows where you are.</h2>
      <p>Most of us ride out alone more often than we admit, and &ldquo;the top field, past the second gate&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t much use to an ambulance.</p>
      <p>One tap on SOS sends your exact location to your emergency contact &mdash; the coordinates and a map link they can tap to see precisely where you are &mdash; and offers to call 999. It asks you to hold it down first &mdash; a phone rattling about in a saddlebag shouldn&rsquo;t be able to call out on your behalf.</p>
      <p>It works on GPS, so it doesn&rsquo;t need a phone signal to know where you are.</p>
    </div>
